# Test Files — Placement and Naming

Follow the documented test structure. Do not put test files in the wrong location or use the wrong naming.

## Where test files go

### Components (web and mobile)

- **Colocated with the component:** `ComponentName/ComponentName.test.tsx` (same folder as `ComponentName.tsx`).
- **Do not** put component tests in a separate `__tests__/` folder at the app root; keep them next to the component.
- **Naming:** `ComponentName.test.tsx` — same base name as the component file, with `.test.tsx` (or `.test.ts` if the component is `.ts`).
- **Required:** Every component MUST have a test file. When adding a new component, add `ComponentName.test.tsx` in the same folder.

### Utils (mobile: apps/mobile-app/utils)

- **Dedicated test folder:** `utils/__tests__/utilityName.test.ts`.
- **Naming:** `utilityName.test.ts` — matches the util file name.
- **Required:** All utils must have tests in `utils/__tests__/`. See `apps/mobile-app/docs/project-structure.md`.

### Utils (shared: packages/shared)

- **Colocated under the module:** e.g. `packages/shared/src/utils/__tests__/newUtility.test.ts`. See `packages/shared/docs/contributing-guide.md`.

### Hooks and services

- **Mobile/web:** No single mandated folder; follow the app’s existing pattern. If the app uses colocated tests (e.g. next to the hook or in a `__tests__` folder under the same area), match that. When in doubt, use a colocated `useHookName.test.ts` next to the hook file, or an `__tests__` folder in the same directory as the code under test.

## File naming

- **Extension:** `.test.tsx` for React/JSX tests, `.test.ts` for non-JSX (utils, pure logic).
- **Pattern:** `[sameBaseNameAsSource].test.(ts|tsx)`.
- **Do not** use `.spec.` in this project; use `.test.` only.

## Imports in test files

- **Component tests:** Import the component under test with a **relative path** (e.g. `import ComponentName from "./ComponentName";`). Do not use `@/components` for the component under test when the test lives inside `components/`. See `docs/import-patterns-guide.md`.
- **Utils tests:** Import from the relative path to the util (e.g. `import { fn } from "../utilityName";`).

## What to test (summary)

- **Do:** Rendering, user interactions, business logic, error handling, edge cases.
- **Do not:** Implementation details, third-party library behavior, framework internals.
- **Placeholders:** Skip tests for placeholder components/pages until they are built out. Add tests when the component is implemented. See `docs/testing-strategy.md`.

## Running tests

- **Mobile:** `yarn test` (from repo root or `apps/mobile-app`), `yarn test:ci`, `yarn test:coverage`, `yarn test:watch`.
- **Web:** Same commands from `apps/web-app`.
- **Shared:** `yarn test:shared` or the shared package test script.

Source of truth: `docs/testing-strategy.md`, `docs/component-organization-guide.md`, and each app’s `docs/project-structure.md`.
